1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,000
Setting up your Daily View screen
takes about five minutes.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:11,800
Here's everything you need to do —
no technical experience required.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
You'll need three things:

4
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:21,500
the screen, its charger, and your own
phone or computer.

5
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:27,500
You'll set this up from your Daily View
account, not from the screen.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
First, plug in the screen and turn it on.

7
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:44,500
Connect it to your home Wi-Fi, just like
you would with any tablet.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Next, open a web browser on the screen

9
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:57,500
and go to [SCREEN URL].

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,500
While you're there, add it to the
home screen.

11
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:10,500
That way, next time the screen restarts,
Daily View opens automatically —

12
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,500
no need to type the address again.

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,500
You'll now see a screen that says
"Connect this screen,"

14
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:26,500
with a box waiting for a code.

15
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:31,500
Leave this open — we'll come back
to it in a moment.

16
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,500
Now pick up your own phone or computer,

17
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:44,000
and log into your Daily View dashboard.

18
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:49,500
Go to Devices, and select Add device.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,500
Give the screen a name, so it's easy
to recognize later —

20
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:01,500
something like "Mum's kitchen screen"
works well.

21
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:07,000
Then you'll see a short code,
along with a QR code.

22
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:11,500
This code stays valid for fifteen minutes.

23
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,500
Type that code into the box
on the screen,

24
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:24,500
and select Connect.

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:31,000
That's it — the screen now shows
today's plan automatically,

26
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:36,000
and it will keep itself up to date
from here on.

27
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:42,500
Find a stable spot for it — somewhere
it'll stay plugged in

28
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:47,500
and easy to glance at — and you're done.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,500
If you ever need to make changes,

30
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:59,000
everything is managed from your
Daily View dashboard —

31
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:04,500
the person using the screen never has
to touch a device or account setting.
